      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "### What happened?\n\n```kubeadm reset phase cleanup-node``` prints out some warning messsage: \r\n\r\n> [reset] Failed to remove containers: [failed to stop running pod time=\"2022-06-30T14:55:44+08:00\": output: time=\"2022-06-30T14:55:44+08:00\" level=debug msg=\"get runtime connection\"\r\n\r\n\r\nAnd the pod on that node is not removed eventually.\r\n\r\n\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nall the pods could be removed at last.\n\n### How can we reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)?\n\nHave a crictl installed on the node with the config like this, \r\n```\r\nruntime-endpoint: unix:///var/run/containerd/containerd.sock\r\nimage-endpoint: unix:///var/run/containerd/containerd.sock\r\ntimeout: 2\r\ndebug: true\r\npull-image-on-create: false\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd then run below command, \r\n```kubeadm reset phase cleanup-node```\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Kubernetes version\n\n<details>\r\n```console\r\n$ kubectl version\r\n# paste output here\r\n\r\nmaster\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\n\n### Cloud provider\n\n<details>\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\n\n### OS version\n\n<details>\r\n\r\n```console\r\n# On Linux:\r\n$ cat /etc/os-release\r\n# paste output here\r\n$ uname -a\r\n# paste output here\r\n\r\n# On Windows:\r\nC:\\> wmic os get Caption, Version, BuildNumber, OSArchitecture\r\n# paste output here\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\n\n### Install tools\n\n<details>\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\n\n### Container runtime (CRI) and version (if applicable)\n\n<details>\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\n\n### Related plugins (CNI, CSI, ...) and versions (if applicable)\n\n<details>\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n",
